+# Tend UI Remaining Controls Audit
+
+Date: 2026-07-26
+
+Status: F-43 `[x]`.
+
+## Purpose
+
+Inventory user-facing legacy controls outside the completed column-settings area and divide the remaining work into bounded Tend UI migration waves.
+
+The executable inventory is implemented in:
+
+```text
+scripts/audit-remaining-tend-ui-controls.mjs
+```
+
+It runs inside `npm run verify:tend-ui:all`.
+
+## Inventory
+
+| Area | Remaining controls | Risk | Decision |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Filter drawer actions | Close, Reset, Apply | Low | F-44 first wave |
+| Filter money range | 2 text inputs, 2 range inputs, 3 preset buttons | Medium | Separate wave after actions |
+| Filter multi-select | 8 composite widgets, dynamic options/tags/clear | High | Separate adapter/state design |
+| Filter drawer icons | 18 static inline SVG | Mixed | Remove with owning control waves |
+| System overlay | 3 buttons, 1 input, 5 inline SVG | Medium | Migrate after filter drawer |
+| Task/table dynamic actions | 2 button templates | Medium | Separate row-action wave |
+| Bookmark action | 1 dynamic delete button | Low but conditional | Verify bookmark lifecycle first |
+| Column settings | 0 native controls, 0 inline SVG | Complete | Protected by F-42 gate |
+
+## F-44 Boundary
+
+F-44 will migrate only:
+
+- header Close;
+- footer Reset All;
+- footer Apply.
+
+Tend UI owns `Button`/`Close` presentation and accessible names. Vanilla filter code continues to own:
+
+- drawer and overlay visibility;
+- current filter values and active count;
+- reset behavior while the drawer remains open;
+- Apply, task rerendering, queue/sidebar counts and pagination reset.
+
+Money-range inputs/presets and all multi-select mechanics are explicitly outside F-44.
+
+## Browser Baseline
+
+- all three native F-44 controls are present once;
+- a money preset changes the drawer count to `1` without changing the task list before Apply;
+- Close hides the drawer and preserves the draft value;
+- reopening restores `Выполнено настроек: 1`;
+- Apply closes the drawer and changes the selected queue count `134 -> 27`;
+- Reset changes the drawer count to `0` and keeps the drawer open;
+- the filtered list remains until Reset is followed by Apply;
+- Reset plus Apply restores the queue count `27 -> 134`;
+- visual layout has no overlap;
+- browser application errors are `0`.
+
+## Planned Order
+
+1. F-44: filter drawer Close/Reset/Apply actions.
+2. F-45: money-range text fields and preset actions; range-thumb strategy must be decided explicitly.
+3. F-46: multi-select trigger/options/tags/clear controls.
+4. F-47: system-overlay local controls.
+5. F-48: dynamic task/table actions.
+6. F-49: bookmark delete action after lifecycle verification.
+
+The order after F-44 is provisional and must be revalidated after each completed group.
